Swift J1818.0$-$1607 exhibits an overall average spin-down rate of $\dot{
u} = -1.65(4) 	imes 10^{-11}\,\mathrm{s^{-2}}$ (with piecewise segmented rates spanning from $-6.1(3) 	imes 10^{-12}\,\mathrm{s^{-2}}$ to $-2.03(4) 	imes 10^{-11}\,\mathrm{s^{-2}}$), yielding a characteristic age $	au_{c} = -
u/(2\dot{
u}) \approx 0.71(2)\,\mathrm{kyr}$. The radio two-point spectral index varies widely across $-1.86 \lesssim \alpha \lesssim +0.65$, remaining predominantly hard ($\alpha > -1$) in later epochs. Fifteen robust short-timescale mode-changing events are identified into three phase-dependent classes (Type I central, Type II trailing, Type III leading), accompanied by in-band spectral index shifts (e.g. at 8.60 GHz, $\alpha = +0.77 \pm 0.33$ in State A versus $\alpha = -2.09 \pm 1.32$ in State B).
